    "tree_id": "0512b6da0c86f102c3691757033a7a4c889afa11",
    "message": "Keep new goal baseline aligned with same-day weight corrections (#449)\n\n## Summary\n\nSaving or correcting today's weight after creating a goal could leave\nits starting weight stale. Web/mobile, Wear and imported weights now\nalign the current goal's baseline within their weight transaction,\npreserving goal identity, start day, target, pace and history. The goal\nsync event includes the final safety-review state.\n\nThe existing goal start day (`created_at` in the account timezone),\nmetric date and acceptance-local day must match. The timezone is reread\nafter acquiring the shared planning lock; competing weight writers take\nthat lock before metric rows. A late first offline replay saves its\nmetric without changing an older baseline, while committed retries\nretain their original result.\n\nCloses #446.\n\n## Test plan\n\n| Scenario | Expected and observed result | Evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Create a 90 kg goal, save 85 kg that day, reload Progress | The same\ngoal starts at 85 kg with 0% progress. Before retained 90 kg / 33%;\nAfter shows the correction. | Matched browser captures below; maintained\nmetric regression. |\n| Save weight before goal creation, or while goal creation holds the\nplanning lock | Both orders establish the new baseline without changing\ntarget, pace, date or completed food-day history. | PostgreSQL smoke. |\n| Change timezone while a weight writer waits; test LA/UTC in both\ndirections with explicit/default dates | Eligibility and default date\nuse the committed timezone, and retries retain the receipt. | Forced\nPostgreSQL overlap and controlled-clock route tests. |\n| Overlap web and Wear weight writes in both orders | No lock inversion;\nsuccessful same-day writes correct the baseline and sync it once. Stale\nWear revisions return 409; historical Wear writes retain the baseline.\nWear parses date syntax first; the locked timezone decides eligibility\nin both directions. Newly future dates are rejected without\nmetric/baseline/sync writes; newly current dates are accepted and\ncorrect the baseline. | Forced PostgreSQL overlap. |\n| Import a current-day weight, overwrite it, KEEP it, or repeat a\nhistorical/identical import | Only accepted current-day weight writes\ncorrect the baseline. KEEP, historical rows and identical repeats\nproduce no extra goal correction events. After a concurrent timezone\nchange, accepted/skipped rows, counts and future warnings use the locked\naccount day. | Actual import route and ZIP parser in PostgreSQL smoke. |\n| Replay after midnight, retry after a newer correction, use pounds,\nfail sync or make a plan unsafe | No historical/stale overwrite;\ncanonical precision, atomic rollback and existing safety-review behavior\nare preserved. | Maintained backend regressions. |\n\nValidation: 61 targeted backend tests passed during the writer-path\nfixes; the final affected Wear suite (14 tests), import suite (6 tests)\nand backend typecheck passed after their narrow follow-ups.\n[Current-head PostgreSQL validation\npassed](https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/actions/runs/37828422760),\nincluding all concurrency and both-direction timezone cases. All\ncurrent-head hosted checks passed: 10 successful, 14 path-filtered\nskips. [Configured review completed with no major\nissues](https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/pull/449#issuecomment-6067011549)\nat this head; all seven prior findings have verified dispositions and\nresolved threads. Earlier unchanged-client validation passed 35 client\ntests, both Expo builds and two browser captures; those unaffected\nsuites were not repeated. Native device testing is deferred.\n[Independent\nQA](https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/pull/449#issuecomment-6067634380)\npassed code, review dispositions, applicable CI and evidence checks;\nfinal description reassessment remains pending.\n\nThe screenshots show a synthetic API correction followed by the actual\nProgress UI reload. They use the real metric route with synthetic\npersistence; unrelated trend/target/projection values are fixtures. They\ndo not establish native or real database behavior.\n\nActual target master is `9dc0739e36168aa273530fe00ae5f85fb9c8a3fe` after\nPR436 merged. Historical merge-base and captured Before:\n`4cbcbc740fbe5fa5646b4de31951c79a653176d5`. Captured After:\n`eb142dd0bcc527398e83b91d29d4514fd9b4e516`. Current head:\n`650862e1c13be66fe5ec05495320cc66ac32f8bb`. Later fixes preserve the\ncaptured stable-timezone scenario; the old images are not relabeled as\nnew-head captures. The [independent target-impact\nassessment](https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/blob/124f0906831b6d97ea09463ca3b4a1f0f6a95ab3/verdict.json)\nfound PR436's incoming changes integrate without textual conflict and\npreserve the goal-baseline behavior and original capture applicability.\n\n| Before | After |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Before: stale 90 kg\nbaseline](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/ce02f46f2d6b3794d3911a74a7c29a63ac6960c4/before.png)\n| ![After: corrected 85 kg\nbaseline](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/ce02f46f2d6b3794d3911a74a7c29a63ac6960c4/after.png)\n|\n\n[Original captures, build manifests and immutable\nprovenance](https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/tree/ce02f46f2d6b3794d3911a74a7c29a63ac6960c4)\nand [final source binding, review-fix evidence and capture\napplicability](https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/blob/458ff9fa117ca51b2c07c565069d809ecb8518d5/final-source-binding.md)\nare retained outside product history. All earlier evidence records\nremain accessible. Implementation-owner and independent QA pixel\ninspection completed; the independent assessment verified original\nprovenance and current-source/target applicability. [The previous\ndescription](https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/pull/449#issuecomment-6067666764)\nis preserved.",
